  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_020 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) at 0.713 acc. All four completed experiments use resnet50 as the image encoder, so the impact of a stronger image encoder is completely untested. The multiprofile + transformer + weighted combination is clearly the winning architecture (0.713 vs 0.540 singleprofile, 0.678 avgpool, 0.688 concat). Question: Does upgrading the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l improve accuracy in this proven-best multimodal setup? config_010 is config_020 with only the image encoder changed, isolating this single variable. Rationale: The image encoder is the largest untested design axis, and ViT-L is substantially more expressive than ResNet50; if it helps, it could push accuracy well above 0.713. With 5 experiments left, identifying whether the larger encoder is worth its cost is the highest-value uncertainty to resolve. Expected relative cost: higher than config_020 (6.22 GPU hrs) due to the larger ViT-L backbone, likely ~9-12 GPU hrs, but justified because it tests the most promising accuracy lever."
}

